{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"An individual term of a series is the difference between two successive partial sums.\n\nIn particular, $\\displaystyle{{a}_{n}}={{S}_{n}}-{{S}_{n-1}}\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\\displaystyle{{S}_{n}}-{{S}_{n-1}}\u0026=\\left(2+\\dfrac{3n+1}{4n}\\right)-\\left(2+\\dfrac{3(n-1)+1}{4(n-1)}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\displaystyle ~=\\frac{3n+1}{4n}-\\frac{3n-2}{4(n-1)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\displaystyle ~=\\frac{(3n+1)(n-1)-n(3n-2)}{4n(n-1)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\displaystyle ~=\\frac{-1}{4n(n-1)}\n\\end{align}$\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"The $n\\text{th}$ partial sum of the series $\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{{a}_{n}}}$ is given by\n\n$\\displaystyle{{S}_{n}}=2+\\frac{3n+1}{4n}$.\n\n**Write a rule for ${{a}_{n}}$.**\n\n[[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"-1/((n4)(n-1))"}],"buttonSets":["basic"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
